{
  format: 1
  name: string-search-wrong-arity-rejected-at-load
  suite: static
  spec: ["#expressions", "§6.5"]
  note: '''
    Attack: call a search predicate with one argument, hoping the engine treats
    the missing needle as empty (which would make the check vacuously true, since
    §6.5 makes the empty needle a prefix of everything) or as `none`.

    §6.5: `string.starts_with` takes two `text` arguments, and "a call supplying
    other than two arguments is a static (load-time) error: the arity is part of
    the signature package loading validates". §6.5 likewise: "Package loading
    validates every function name, type, determinism class, and namespace
    contract." The package must therefore be rejected at load, not accepted with
    a silently-defaulted argument.
  '''

  package: {
    $liasse: 1
    $app: "t.strarity@1.0.0"
    $model: {
      accounts: {
        $key: "code"
        code: {
          $type: "text"
          $check: ["string.starts_with(.)", "A code needs a prefix"]
        }
      }
    }
  }

  expect: {
    outcome: invalid
    violates: ["#expressions", "§6.5"]
    detail: "string.starts_with takes two arguments, but one was supplied"
  }
}
